// Branching on a command's reply — the script shape real automation needs.
//
// `case` and `if` are check-only (they need an expected type), and an
// expression-only script has no `def` signature to carry one. The
// computation-sorted ascription `(t : F A)` fills that hole: it elaborates
// through the thunk annotation (`force ((thunk t) : U_ω (F A))`), so the
// `if` below is checked against `F String` and the script stays a single
// expression item.
//
// `test -d /tmp` exits zero exactly when the directory exists, so the
// reply's `exit_code` field drives the branch through the prelude's `==`.
{
  run probe <- #!{ test -d /tmp; };
  (if probe.exit_code == 0 { ret "present" } else { ret "absent" } : F String)
}

// The harness checks:
//@ mode: shell
//@ expect-shell-value: "present"
